       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nIbuprofen 4000 mg four times daily is 16,000 mg/day. That is about 5 times the maximum daily dose for adults. The usual maximum is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use, given as 400\u2013800 mg per dose, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use. A dose that high could cause serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and metabolic acidosis, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg** PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg** PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- **4000 mg/day total**, which is also above the maximum and which I'd advise against\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 4000 mg per dose, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
